{
  "dom_id": "step-q338464",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ are\n\n${x}_{1}=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Note that the function $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is not defined at $x={90}^{∘},\\,{270}^{∘}.$\n\nFirst, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the zero-product property, we have to solve two equations:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}=0\n$$\n\nLet's solve each equation separately.\n\n- First, we solve $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0.$ The solutions to this equation for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ are $x={90}^{∘},\\,{270}^{∘}.$\n\n- Then, we solve $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}=0,$ or equivalently $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}.$ The solutions to this equation for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ are $x={120}^{∘},\\,{300}^{∘}.$\n\nTaking into account that ${90}^{∘}$ and ${270}^{∘}$ are excluded values, and arranging the remaining solutions in ascending order, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={120}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={300}^{∘}.\n$$",
